WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Oil sands operations contribute significant carbon emissions in Canada. So the six largest companies have teamed up to make strides on the path to NetZero. Investing in technology and innovation. Already cut emissions in average 22% per barrel. Working with governments to create and protect jobs. Developing one of the world's largest carbon capture and storage facilities. Our NetZero plan is in motion and we're making progress on multiple pathways. See our plan in action at PathwaysAlliance.ca
加拿大油砂开采产生了大量的碳排放。因此，六家最大的公司携手合作，在通往净零排放的道路上取得进展。他们投资于技术和创新，已将每桶石油的平均碳排放量降低了22%。他们与政府合作以创造和保护就业机会，并正在建设世界最大的碳捕集与封存设施之一。我们的净零计划正在实施中，我们正通过多种途径取得进展。请访问 PathwaysAlliance.ca 了解我们付诸实践的计划。

2
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:56.000
Cindy Paulson stood alone on the corner of East 4th Avenue and Denali Street in downtown Anchorage. 18-year-old Cindy was a sex worker who frequented the city's infamous Tenderloin district. With its array of bars and clubs, the area was typically a hotbed of potential clients. But so far, the night of Sunday June 12 1983 had been a quiet one. Then, shortly before midnight, a green Buick sentry pulled up to the curb where Cindy stood. The male driver peered up at her from behind a pair of thick rimmed eyeglasses. He propositioned Cindy and the pair began negotiating. After they'd settled on a price, Cindy climbed into the car's passenger seat.
辛迪·保尔森独自站在安克雷奇市中心东第四大道和杰纳利街的街角。18岁的辛迪是一名性工作者，经常出没于该市臭名昭著的红灯区。这里有着各种酒吧和俱乐部，通常是潜在客户聚集的热点。但截至1983年6月12日星期日晚，这天晚上一直很安静。接着，就在午夜之前，一辆绿色的别克世纪轿车停在了辛迪站立的路边。男司机透过一副厚框眼镜抬头看着她。他向辛迪搭讪，两人开始谈价钱。在敲定价格后，辛迪坐上了汽车的副驾驶座。

3
00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:50.000
The man drove her to a secluded parking lot and turned off the engine. Within seconds, he'd produced a wood-handled 357 Magnum revolver. Aiming at Cindy with one hand, he grabbed a pair of handcuffs from under his seat with the other. A smile crept across his pockmarked face as he restrained Cindy's wrists. We're going to my house, he told her. He drove east along the Glen Highway where the city's lights and noise were soon replaced by the dark stillness of suburbia. Turning down a cul-de-sac named Old Harbour Avenue, they passed several ranch-like family homes before pulling into a driveway that led to a single story blue-gray weatherboard house.
这名男子把车开到一个偏僻的停车场，并熄了发动机。几秒钟之内，他掏出了一把带木柄的 .357 马格南左轮手枪。他一只手用枪指着辛迪，另一只手从座位底下抓出一副手铐。他的麻脸上露出一丝微笑，同时铐住了辛迪的手腕。我们要去我家，他对她说。他沿着格伦高速公路向东开去，市里的灯光和噪音很快就被郊区黑暗的寂静所取代。驶入一条名为旧港大道的 cul-de-sac（尽头路）后，他们路过了几栋牧场风格的家庭住宅，然后驶入了一条车道，车道通向一栋单层的蓝灰色木瓦平房。

4
00:02:50.000 --> 00:03:38.000
A pair of antlers hung above the door of a two-car garage. To its right was the main living area, with several windows overlooking the front lawn. No one stirred within. The remainder of the spacious property was equally silent and still, shadowed by tall aspen and birch trees. Dragging Cindy inside the house, the man took her down some stairs into a wood-paneled basement. What first caught her attention were all the taxidermied animals and hunting trophies that filled the room. Rainbirds, mountain goats, dull sheep and caribou had been stuffed and mounted throughout.
一对手鹿角挂在一个双车库的门上方。它的右边是主要起居区，有几扇窗户俯瞰着前院。里面毫无动静。这处宽敞房产的其余部分同样寂静无声，在高大的白杨树和桦树的阴影下显得格外安静。这名男子把辛迪拖进屋里，带她顺着楼梯走下一间木质镶板的地下室。首先引起她注意的是填满整个房间的各种动物标本和狩猎战利品。雷鸟、山羊、盘羊和北美驯鹿被制成标本，挂满了整个房间。

5
00:03:38.000 --> 00:04:56.000
Walrus tusks and moose antlers decorated the walls. Beaver and wolf hides were scattered about. On the floor was a baskin rug. In a moment of crystal-clear clarity, Cindy realised that she was trapped in the lair of a man who liked killing. Retrieving a chain, the man wrapped it around Cindy's neck four times before locking it against a wooden support beam. Then he raped her, before settling down for a nap on a nearby sofa. Pointing his revolver at Cindy, he warned her not to wake him or quote, You'll make me mad, and you don't want to see me mad.
海象牙和驼鹿角装饰着墙壁。海狸和狼的皮毛散落各处。地板上铺着一张熊皮地毯。在某一瞬间，辛迪脑海中异常清晰地意识到，自己被困在了一个喜欢杀戮的男子的巢穴里。男子取出一根链条，在辛迪的脖子上绕了四圈，然后将其锁在一根木质支撑梁上。接着，他强奸了她，随后在附近的沙发上安顿下来打盹。他用左轮手枪指着辛迪，警告她不要吵醒他，或者原话是：“你会惹我生气的，你不会想看到我生气的样子。”

6
00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:44.000
While her captor slept, Cindy's mind raced. Her eyes darted around the basement, taking in every detail. There was a pool table and foosball table, a television, a clock, a computer, a rack of women's clothing and all of those dead animals. Cindy knew with absolute certainty that they hadn't been her captor's only victims. She thought about grabbing one of the pool cues and hitting him over the head. But what if he died? She'd be trapped down there, still chained to the beam with no way of calling for help. Or worse, she might not hit him hard enough and he would kill her then and there.
趁着绑架者睡觉时，辛迪的大脑飞速运转。她的目光在地下室里四处扫视，将每一个细节都收入眼底。这里有台球桌和手足球台、一台电视机、一个时钟、一台电脑、一排女装以及所有那些死去的动物。辛迪百分之百确定，这些绝对不是她绑架者的唯一受害者。她想过随手抓起一根台球杆砸他的头。但如果他死了呢？她就会被困在下面，依然被锁在柱子上，无法呼救。或者更糟糕的是，她可能没能狠狠地击中他，而他就会当场杀死她。

7
00:05:44.000 --> 00:06:37.000
Instead, Cindy waited in silence until the man stirred awake. He unchained her, but kept the handcuffs secured around her wrists. Under the static, lifeless stairs of the animals perched around them, he bragged of his world record hunting success and showed off one of his trophies. Then he raped Cindy again on the bare skin rug. Afterwards, his conversation took an even more sinister turn. The man explained how he had brought seven other women to his house, all of whom he kept captive for a week. In an attempt to appeal to his humanity, Cindy tearfully begged to be released so she could see her mother again.
相反，辛迪静静地等待着，直到那名男子醒来。他解开了她的链条，但让手铐依然锁在她的手腕上。在死寂的楼梯下和周围栖息的动物标本注视下，他吹嘘自己世界纪录般的狩猎战绩，并展示了其中一个战利品。接着，他在光秃秃的熊皮地毯上再次强奸了辛迪。事后，他的谈话内容变得更加险恶。这名男子解释说，他曾把另外七名女性带到他家，并将她们每人软禁了一个星期。为了唤醒他的仁慈，辛迪泪流满面地哀求他放她走，好让她能再见到母亲。

8
00:06:37.000 --> 00:07:29.000
Everything's gonna be okay, he reassured her. I'm not going to hurt you. He said that he'd only brought Cindy to his home because he wanted to get his money's worth. But now he liked her so much that he wanted to take her to a remote cabin he owned where they could, quote, make love one more time before he let her go. He owned a plane that he kept at Merrill Field Airport so they could fly out from there. Cindy nodded along, pretending to be fine with his plan. Yet, she knew the only way she was going to survive was if she found a way to escape.
一切都会好的，他安慰她。我不会伤害你的。他说，他把辛迪带回家只是因为想物有所值。但现在他太喜欢她了，想带她去他名下的一间偏远小屋，在那里他们可以——原话是——“再做爱一次”，然后他就放她走。他有一架飞机，停放在梅里尔菲尔德机场，这样他们就可以从那里飞走。辛迪连连点头，假装同意他的计划。然而，她心里清楚，自己能够生还的唯一方法就是找到逃跑的办法。

9
00:07:29.000 --> 00:08:22.000
The sun hadn't yet risen when Cindy was led from the weatherboard house and back into the Buick. She was forced to lie down along the back seat where she was covered with an army blanket. As her captor drove, Cindy remembered that Merrill Field was right by the motel where she was staying with her boyfriend. If she managed to get away somehow, she wouldn't have to run far for help. They arrived at the airport shortly before 5am. Private bush planes lined the acres of quiet, dark field. Cindy's captor pulled up near a blue and white two-seater Super Cub. He got out and began loading the aircraft with things from the trunk of his car.
太阳还没升起，辛迪就被带出木瓦房，重新塞回别克车里。她被迫躺在后座上，身上盖着一条军毯。在绑架者开车时，辛迪记起梅里尔菲尔德机场就在她和男友住的汽车旅馆旁边。如果她能设法逃脱，她就不需要跑很远去求救。他们在凌晨5点前不久抵达机场。私人的丛林飞机排列在数英亩安静黑暗的停机坪上。辛迪的绑架者把车停在一架蓝白相间的双座超级卡布飞机（Super Cub）旁。他下了车，开始把汽车后备箱里的东西往飞机上搬。

10
00:08:22.000 --> 00:09:28.000
Watching from the Buick as he walked back and forth, Cindy suddenly noticed that he'd left the driver's side door ajar. Overcome with nervous energy, she delicately removed her high-heeled shoes, put them aside, and waited. Once the man was over by his plane, Cindy clambered into the front seat and leapt out the open door. Racing barefoot over the gravel runway, Cindy heard the man shout behind her, Stop you bitch or I'll kill you. It took a moment for truck driver Robert Young to register the strange sight before him. A young woman had bolted onto East Fifth Avenue, waving her handcuffed hands in the air and screaming for help. As she sprinted towards Robert's truck, he leaned over to open the passenger side door.
辛迪坐在别克车里看着他来回走动，突然发现他把驾驶员侧的车门留了一条缝。她被紧张的精力所驱使，小心翼翼地脱下高跟鞋，放到一边，然后静静等待。一旦那名男子走到他的飞机旁，辛迪就爬到前座，从开着的门跳了出去。辛迪赤脚在砂石跑道上狂奔，听到身后那名男子大喊：“站住，你这贱人，否则我杀了你。”货车司机罗伯特·杨（Robert Young）花了一会儿才反应过来眼前这诡异的一幕。一名年轻女子冲上了东第五大街，在空中挥舞着戴着手铐的双手，尖叫着寻求帮助。当她向罗伯特的货车冲去时，他探身打开了副驾驶座的车门。

11
00:09:28.000 --> 00:10:35.000
Launching herself inside, the woman yelled, He's going to kill me, get me out of here. According to the book Fair Game, Robert scanned the airfield where the woman had come from but couldn't see who she was referring to. His distressed passenger begged him to hurry, so Robert drove onwards. She asked to be taken to a nearby motel and Robert obliged, pulling over at the mash-in, a low-budget motel 450 feet from Merrill Field. The woman rushed inside. Bewildered, Robert continued driving to work. As soon as he got there, he called the Anchorage Police Department. Ten-year police veteran Greg Baker was halfway through his shift when he got the call to attend the mash-in. By the time he arrived, the handcuffed woman had left in a taxi.
那名女子钻进车里，大喊道：“他要杀了我，带我离开这里。”根据《公平游戏》（Fair Game）一书的记载，罗伯特扫视了女子跑过来的机场，但没有看到她指的是谁。他惊恐的乘客恳求他快点，于是罗伯特继续开车。她要求去附近的汽车旅馆，罗伯特照办了，将车停在距离梅里尔菲尔德机场450英尺的一家名为 Mash-in 的低成本汽车旅馆外。那名女子冲了进去。罗伯特感到困惑，继续开车去上班。一到公司，他就给安克雷奇警察局打了电话。有着十年从警经验的警察格雷格·贝克（Greg Baker）当班正值中途，接到了前往 Mash-in 汽车旅馆的出警电话。等他赶到时，那名戴着手铐的女子已经坐出租车离开了。

12
00:10:35.000 --> 00:11:32.000
She was traced to another motel down the road named The Big Timber. When Officer Baker got there, a front desk clerk directed him to Room 110. He knocked on the door and a young woman answered. She was barefoot and her wrists were red and raw from the handcuffs still clasped around them. Her name was Cindy Paulson. After hearing of her ordeal, Officer Baker escorted Cindy to hospital to undergo an examination. As they drove by Merrill Field, she insisted on showing him her assailant's aircraft. She singled out a blue and white Super Cub, which bore a registration number on its tail, written as small as regulations allowed.
警方顺藤摸瓜，追踪到马路对面另一家名为“大森林”（The Big Timber）的汽车旅馆。当贝克警官赶到那里时，前台接待员把他指引到了110房间。他敲了敲门，一名年轻女子应门。她赤着脚，手腕由于被紧紧铐着而红肿破皮。她的名字叫辛迪·保尔森。在听取了她的悲惨遭遇后，贝克警官护送辛迪前往医院接受检查。当他们开车经过梅里尔菲尔德机场时，她坚持要向他展示她袭击者的飞机。她认出了一架蓝白相间的超级卡布飞机，其机尾上印有一个注册号，字体小到了法规允许的极限。

13
00:11:32.000 --> 00:12:34.000
Upon cross-checking the plane's registration, police discovered it belonged to a man who lived at the Old Harbor Avenue address where Cindy said she had been held captive. Police rushed to the blue-gray weatherboard house only to discover that no one was home. They stood guard over the property and waited. Shortly before 7am, a green Buick sentry pulled into the driveway. Officers descended on the vehicle and its driver, 44-year-old Robert Hanson. Originally from Iowa, Hanson had moved to Alaska with his wife in 1963. The couple settled in Anchorage where they had two children. Hanson had followed in his father's footsteps by becoming a baker and owned the business Hanson's Bakery a few blocks from downtown.
通过交叉核对飞机的注册信息，警方发现它属于一名男子，该男子居住在辛迪所说的她被囚禁的旧港大道地址。警方冲进那栋蓝灰色的木瓦房，却发现空无一人。他们在房产周围把守并等待着。清晨7点前不久，一辆绿色的别克世纪轿车驶入车道。警员们包围了这辆车及其司机——44岁的罗伯特·汉森（Robert Hanson）。汉森原籍艾奥瓦州，于1963年随妻子移居阿拉斯加。这对夫妇在安克雷奇定居并育有两名子女。汉森子承父业成为了一名面包师，并在距离市中心几个街区的地方拥有一家名为“汉森面包店”的生意。

14
00:12:34.000 --> 00:13:21.000
Anchorage police were very familiar with Robert Hanson, known locally as Bob. His bakery wasn't far from the station, so they visited often for coffee and donuts. Hanson was, by all accounts, a stable and religious family man. During his youth, he had been enlisted in the US military and he'd since become an active member of the community. Hanson was unarmed when police surrounded his vehicle. Calmly, he asked them, What can I do for you officers? Cindy Paulson had accurately detailed his appearance and even knew of his stutter.
安克雷奇警方对罗伯特·汉森非常熟悉，当地人称他为鲍勃。他的面包店离警察局不远，所以他们经常去那里喝咖啡吃甜甜圈。根据所有人的说法，汉森是一个稳定且有宗教信仰的顾家好男人。年轻时，他曾应征加入美军，此后一直积极参与社区活动。警方包围他的车辆时，汉森身上没有武器。他平静地问他们：“警官，我能为你们做点什么吗？”辛迪·保尔森准确地描述了他的外貌，甚至知道他口吃。

15
00:13:21.000 --> 00:14:15.000
A bright green baseball cap and green coat were spotted in his car, matching what Cindy said he was wearing when he picked her up. Her descriptions of his house, inside and out, were also spot on. Hanson signed a waiver allowing police to search his car, home and aircraft. There was nothing of evidentiary value in his buick. Cindy's shoes, which she had left behind as evidence of her presence, were not in the vehicle. There was nothing to prove she'd been held captive in Hanson's house, either. The basement full of hunting paraphernalia was just as Cindy described, but there was no wooden beam like the one she'd said she was chained to overnight, nor was there even a chain.
在他的车里发现了一顶亮绿色的棒球帽和一件绿色外套，这与辛迪所说他接她时穿的衣服相符。她对他的房子内外结构的描述也分毫不差。汉森签署了一份豁免书，允许警方搜查他的汽车、住宅和飞机。他的别克车里没有发现具有证据价值的物品。辛迪作为她存在证据而遗留的鞋子并不在车内。也没有任何证据证明她曾被关押在汉森的家里。摆满狩猎用品的地下室正如辛迪所描述的那样，但并没有她所说自己被链子锁过夜的那根木梁，甚至连链子也没有。

16
00:14:15.000 --> 00:15:12.000
Also missing were a yellow towel and washcloth Cindy claimed to have used. A search of Hanson's Super Cub was equally anticlimactic. Hanson was an award-winning trophy hunter who owned an array of pistols, rifles and shotguns, but none matched the wood-handled revolver used against Cindy. Hanson agreed to be interviewed and was polite and cooperative throughout. He denied abducting or raping Cindy Paulson and had an alibi to prove it. Half an hour before Cindy was abducted, Hanson went to the home of a friend named John Henning. He remained there all night, staying up with John until 5.30am drinking beer and planning a fishing trip.
同样不见踪影的还有辛迪声称自己用过的黄色毛巾和洗脸巾。对汉森的超级卡布飞机的搜查同样波澜不惊。汉森是一位屡获殊荣的战利品猎人，拥有一系列手枪、步枪和猎枪，但没有一把符合对辛迪使用的那支木柄左轮手枪。汉森同意接受讯问，并在整个过程中表现得礼貌且配合。他否认绑架或强奸了辛迪·保尔森，并有不在场证明来证明这一点。在辛迪被绑架前半小时，汉森去了名叫约翰·亨宁（John Henning）的朋友家。他在那里待了一整晚，和约翰一直熬夜到凌晨5:30，一边喝啤酒一边计划一次垂钓之旅。

17
00:15:12.000 --> 00:16:09.000
Afterwards, they headed to Merrill Field to install a seat in Hanson's Super Cub. John Henning confirmed Hanson's assertions. A physical examination of Cindy Paulson revealed evidence of vaginal penetration along with the presence of semen. But the examining doctor told investigators that Cindy only had abrasions around her wrists, not her neck, where she said a chain had been looped. Despite this, Cindy maintained her version of events. With Hanson's whereabouts fully accounted for, investigators presumed that Cindy was lying in some capacity. It was clear from her accurate description of both Robert Hanson and his property that Cindy knew him in some way,
之后，他们前往梅里尔菲尔德机场，为汉森的超级卡布飞机安装一个座位。约翰·亨宁证实了汉森的说法。对辛迪·保尔森的身体检查显示有阴道穿透的迹象以及精液的存在。但负责检查的医生告诉调查人员，辛迪的手腕周围有擦伤，但脖子上却没有——她曾说链条曾套在脖子上。尽管如此，辛迪仍然坚持自己的说法。由于汉森的行踪有完整的解释，调查人员推测辛迪在某些方面撒了谎。从她对罗伯特·汉森及其住所的准确描述中，很明显辛迪在某种程度上认识他，

18
00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:58.000
likely through her sex work. But whatever had happened to her the previous night, it couldn't have been at his hands. She likely did meet with a client, though the ordeal she described didn't add up. While Hanson was cagey about any history he might have had with Cindy Paulson, she was adamant that they had met once before. Cindy mentioned that Hanson had propositioned her previously from his Buick. As detailed in the book Fair Game, he had introduced himself using a different name. The two arranged to meet the night before her abduction, but he was a no-show.
