一张巨大的卡尼克河谷地图被钉在墙上。在一个大圆圈内画了两个X。旁边用全大写字母潦草地写着这样几个字：“在此区域内识别出汉森”。在被护送进房间后，汉森独自留在那里一会儿，以便他能将这一切尽收眼底。不久，格伦·弗洛维大步走进房间，开始了审讯。尽管汉森承认自己有犯罪前科，但他坚称那都已经是过去式了。审讯持续了数小时，涵盖了汉森历史的方方面面，

32
00:33:07.000 --> 00:34:05.000
from his initial charges of arson and theft to the allegations of abduction and rape. Interviewing officers stopped short of mentioning the murders for now. They discussed Hanson's first known offence against a woman, the botched abduction of an anchorage teenager from her apartment in 1971. When apprehended for this crime, Hanson claimed he had blacked out and therefore had no recollection of the event. As he sat before Sergeant Flovey in an interrogation room adorned with the faces of missing or murdered women, Hanson admitted that he had never really suffered any memory blackout in his life. According to the book Fair Game, this admission likely stemmed from Hanson knowing he wouldn't face any consequences
从他最初的纵火和盗窃指控到绑架和强奸的指控。审讯警官目前暂且没有提及谋杀案。他们讨论了汉森针对女性的第一起已知罪行——1971年从安克雷奇一处公寓未遂绑架一名十几岁女孩的案件。当因这起罪行被捕时，汉森声称自己当时失去了意识，因此对该事件毫无记忆。当他坐在审讯室里面对弗洛维警长时，周围装饰着失踪或被谋杀女性的面孔，汉森承认他一生中从未真正经历过任何记忆黑洞。根据《公平游戏》一书的记载，这种供认很可能源于汉森知道十多年后揭露真相也不会面临任何后果，

33
00:34:05.000 --> 00:34:51.000
for revealing the truth more than a decade later. But it did expose him as a liar. Soon, the line of questioning turned to Sherry Morrow. When shown a photograph of the murdered 23-year-old, Hanson asked, Who's that? He refused to admit any knowledge of her murder or Paula Gouldings. He did say that he occasionally visited the areas where their bodies were found before adding, I didn't shoot anybody. I would not hurt anybody.
但这确实暴露了他是一个骗子的事实。很快，盘问的焦点转向了雪莉·莫罗。当被展示一张被害23岁女孩的照片时，汉森问：“那是谁？”他拒绝承认自己对她或保拉·古尔丁的谋杀有任何了解。他确实说过，他偶尔会去发现他们尸体的地方，然后又补充道：“我没有枪杀任何人。我不会伤害任何人。”

34
00:34:51.000 --> 00:35:45.000
Meanwhile, police swarmed Robert Hanson's home and workplace to execute a search warrant. Word of their presence quickly spread to the disbelief of his family and friends. They had yet to learn why authorities had honed in on the seemingly stable and neighbourly Hanson and couldn't comprehend the idea that he might be in trouble with the law. The police activity soon peaked the interest of Joan, the wife of Hanson's close friend, John Henning. She wondered whether their efforts related to something her husband had told her several months earlier. Shortly after a panicked Cindy Paulson had run handcuffed and barefoot from Merrill Field Airport, Robert Hanson made a phone call.
与此同时，警方蜂拥至罗伯特·汉森的家和工作场所执行搜查令。他们出现的消息迅速传开，令他的家人和朋友感到难以置信。他们还没弄明白为什么当局会把目标锁定在看似稳重且有邻家风范的汉森身上，无法理解他会惹上官司的想法。警方的行动很快激起了汉森挚友约翰·亨宁的妻子琼（Joan）的兴趣。她想知道他们的行动是否与她丈夫几个月前告诉她的事情有关。就在惊恐的辛迪·保尔森戴着手铐赤脚从梅里尔菲尔德机场逃跑后不久，罗伯特·汉森打了一通电话。

35
00:35:45.000 --> 00:36:30.000
It was around 5.30am when John Henning picked up the receiver to hear Hanson, his longtime friend, on the other line. Hanson asked if they could meet at his bakery right away. John was confused but agreed. When John arrived, Hanson told him how his wife and children were overseas and in an effort to overcome loneliness, he had picked up a sex worker. He took her back to his house where they had sex before she raised the price of her services. Hanson wouldn't pay and now she was seeking revenge by falsely accusing him of rape.
大约凌晨5点30分，约翰·亨宁拿起话筒，听到他的老朋友汉森在电话那头。汉森问他们是否可以马上在面包店见面。约翰感到困惑但还是同意了。约翰到达后，汉森告诉他，由于妻子和孩子在海外，为了克服孤独，他接了一名性工作者。他把她带回自己家，两人发生性关系后，她提高了性服务的价格。汉森不肯付钱，现在她通过虚假指控他强奸来进行报复。

36
00:36:30.000 --> 00:37:30.000
Hanson started as he spoke. He was clearly very anxious. Fearing he might be arrested, he told John he didn't want his family to find out and be hurt by his adultery. He asked if John would give him an alibi for 11.30pm until 5.30am. The timeframe in which Cindy Paulson was abducted held captive and taken to the airfield. John believed Hanson and like many others, he dismissed the incident as a trick gone awry. To help his friend, John confirmed his alibi when police came knocking. As John was a well-respected local businessman, his statement was given considerable credibility. John had told his wife about the favour he'd done for his friend.
汉森说话时有些结巴，显然非常焦虑。唯恐自己被捕，他告诉约翰他不想让家人发现并因他的通奸行为而受到伤害。他请求约翰为他在晚上11点30分到凌晨5点30分之间提供不在场证明。这个时间段正是辛迪·保尔森被绑架、软禁并被带到机场的时间。约翰相信了汉森，和许多其他人一样，他把这起事件轻描淡写地看作是一次搞砸了的嫖娼交易。为了帮助朋友，当警察找上门来时，约翰证实了他的不在场证明。由于约翰是当地备受尊敬的商界人士，他的证词被赋予了相当高的可信度。约翰曾将自己为朋友做的好事告诉了妻子。

37
00:37:30.000 --> 00:38:17.000
As described in the book Butcher Baker, when John heard that Hanson's properties were being searched, she got in her car and cruised past Hanson's residence. Upon seeing the heavy police presence and speaking with officers at the scene, she realised it was time for her husband to come clean. John Henning contacted investigators and admitted that he'd provided a false alibi for Hanson on the night of Cindy Paulson's abduction and rape. Henning thought he'd been looking out for Hanson and his family by covering for him. He had no idea how serious the incident had actually been.
正如《屠夫面包师》一书中所描述的那样，当约翰听到汉森的房产正在被搜查时，她坐上车，从汉森的住宅前驶过。在看到大批警察并与现场警官交谈后，她意识到是时候让丈夫说出真相了。约翰·亨宁联系了调查人员，承认自己在辛迪·保尔森被绑架和强奸的当晚为汉森提供了虚假的不在场证明。亨宁以为他为汉森和他的家人作掩护是在照顾他们。他根本不知道这起事件实际上有多么严重。

38
00:38:17.000 --> 00:38:55.000
Despite now having no alibi for the night Cindy Paulson was attacked, Robert Hanson still denied being involved. It didn't matter. Police had enough evidence now to charge him with Cindy's abduction and rape. He was remanded on a $500,000 bond. Hanson's Old Harbor Avenue property was teeming with state troopers, searching for any evidence to link him to other crimes. The houses' communal rooms were neat and organised.
尽管现在没有了辛迪·保尔森遇袭当晚的不在场证明，罗伯特·汉森仍然否认自己参与其中。这已经无关紧要了。警方现在有足够的证据以辛迪的绑架和强奸罪起诉他。他被还押候审，保释金为50万美元。汉森的旧港大道房产里挤满了州警，他们正在搜寻任何能将他与其他罪行联系起来的证据。房子里的公共房间井然有序、干净整洁。

39
00:38:55.000 --> 00:39:36.000
In the living area, knickknacks were arranged in tidy rows on shelves and had couches framed a small coffee table. Family photos lined the hallway, as did a portrait of Jesus Christ. Searching some cupboards, officers found elastic bandages and a bag full of cash. Shotguns and rifles were recovered from a closet in the living room and a hidden cabinet. Given that Hanson had been previously convicted of a felony, he was forbidden by law to possess any firearms. He would be charged accordingly.
在起居区，小摆设在架子上整齐地排列成行，沙发环绕着一张小茶几。走廊里挂满了家庭照片，还有一幅耶稣基督的画像。搜查了一些橱柜后，警官们发现了弹性绷带和一袋现金。起居室的壁橱和一个隐藏的柜子里搜出了猎枪和步枪。鉴于汉森先前有重罪定罪，法律禁止他拥有任何枪支。他将为此受到相应的指控。

40
00:39:36.000 --> 00:40:15.000
There was also a strange kit that contained tools for creating disguises, including a fake mustache, nail polish and skin adhesive. A number of stolen goods were discovered, indicating Hanson's kleptomania had never gone away. The troopers made their way downstairs to the basement, where Cindy Paulson said she'd been held captive. They made their way around the room, carefully pressing against the wood-panelled walls. One portion suddenly gave way.
还有一个奇怪的工具包，里面包含用于伪装的工具，包括假胡子、指甲油和皮肤粘合剂。还发现了许多赃物，表明汉森的偷窃癖从未消失。州警们来到楼下辛迪·保尔森声称自己被囚禁的地下室。他们在房间四周仔细察看，小心翼翼地按压木质镶板墙壁。其中一部分突然塌陷了。

41
00:40:15.000 --> 00:41:07.000
Behind it was a small, secret room. In its centre was the wooden beam Cindy had described being chained to. After hours of meticulous searching, there was only one area left unexamined, the attic. One trooper offered to climb up into the small, cramped space. Crawling across the beams, he found a stack of animal hides. Continuing onwards, he felt with his hands for anything that might be hidden there. As he pressed into some insulation in one corner, it suddenly collapsed. Beneath it lay several firearms, including a .223 calibre Ruger Mini-14 rifle.
后面是一个狭小的秘密房间。房间中央就是辛迪描述过的拴着链条的那根木梁。经过几个小时的细致搜查，只剩下一个区域没有检查过——阁楼。一名州警主动提出爬进这个狭小局促的空间。他沿着横梁爬行，发现了一叠动物皮毛。继续向前，他用双手摸索着可能藏在那里的任何东西。当他按压一个角落的隔热材料时，它突然坍塌了。下方躺着几把火器，其中包括一支 .223 口径的鲁格 Mini-14 步枪。

42
00:41:07.000 --> 00:42:08.000
There was also a little plastic bag that contained a number of women's rings, watches and necklaces. One had an arrowhead pendant. There was another item found in Hansen's house that was particularly noteworthy. While examining the bedroom he shared with his wife, troopers uncovered a piece of paper stashed behind the bedhead. It was an aeronautical chart, a type of map designed to assist pilots in the navigation of aircraft. The map depicted a huge, sprawling overview of Anchorage and its outskirts. There was the Kinnick River valley to the north of the city, the Kenai Peninsula that jutted out below, and the Port City of Seward further south. The map had been marked with many little black asterisks.
还有一个小塑料袋，里面装着许多女性的戒指、手表和项链。其中一个带有箭头吊坠。在汉森家里还发现了另一件特别引人注目的物品。在检查他和妻子共用的卧室时，州警在床头后面藏着的一张纸被揭晓了。那是一张航空图，一种旨在协助飞行员进行飞机导航的地图。地图上描绘了安克雷奇及其市郊庞大而广阔的全景。北部是基尼克河谷（Kinnick River valley），下方突出的是基奈半岛（Kenai Peninsula），更南部则是港口城市苏厄德（Seward）。地图上标有许多黑色的小星号。

43
00:42:08.000 --> 00:43:25.000
Most of them were dotted along the Kinnick River, though there were many others drawn further out. As Glen Flothey studied the map, it suddenly dawned on him. Hansen had scrawled an asterisk on the exact locations where a Clutner Annie, Joanna Messina, Sherry Morrow and Paula Goulding were found. In total, his map featured 21 such markings. Although Hansen was still only charged with abducting and raping Cindy Paulson, the case was already starting to look like the biggest Alaska had ever seen. Investigators had more evidence of the enormity of his crimes, including Hansen's Ruger rifle, which was confirmed to have fired the bullets that killed Sherry Morrow and Paula Goulding. Furthermore, the friends and families of women missing from Anchorage's Tenderloin district had been shown the items of jewelry hidden in Hansen's attic, many of which were recognized as having belonged to their loved ones.
它们大多点缀在基尼克河沿岸，不过还有许多被标记在更远的地方。当格伦·弗洛西研究这张地图时，他突然明白了。汉森在安妮·克鲁特纳、乔安娜·梅西纳、雪莉·莫罗和宝拉·古尔丁被发现的具体地点潦草地画上了星号。他的地图上一共有21个这样的标记。尽管当时汉森仍只被指控绑架和强奸辛迪·保尔森，但这个案子已经开始显露出阿拉斯加有史以来最大案件的迹象。调查人员掌握了他滔天罪行的更多证据，包括汉森的鲁格步枪，经证实，正是这把枪发射了杀死雪莉·莫罗和宝拉·古尔丁的子弹。此外，安克雷奇特德洛因区失踪女性的朋友和家人们被展示了藏在汉森阁楼里的珠宝，其中许多被认出是他们所爱之人的遗物。

44
00:43:25.000 --> 00:44:35.000
The arrowhead pendant was the spitting image of a necklace that Sherry Morrow was known to wear every single day. Business cards that featured the names of some of the missing women were also discovered in Hansen's garage. Prior to Hansen's arrest, a renowned criminal profiler had stated that the person responsible for the murders would be collecting keepsakes from each of his victims, like a trophy hunter hoarding parts of the animal they had killed as a representation of their success and to relive the hunt from memory. With the evidence against Hansen adding up, it was believed he could be compelled to confess. After some negotiating, a deal was struck with his attorney. If Hansen pleaded guilty to the murders of a Clutner Annie, Joanna Messina, Sherry Morrow and Paula Goulding, then his wife and children would be spared the humiliation and pain of a highly publicized trial.
那枚箭头吊坠与雪莉·莫罗每天佩戴的项链一模一样。在汉森的车库里还发现了印有部分失踪女性名字的名片。在汉森被捕之前，一位著名的犯罪侧写师曾表示，谋杀案的幕后黑手会从每个受害者身上收集纪念品，就像奖杯猎人囤积他们杀死的动物身体部位一样，以此作为成功的象征并从记忆中重温狩猎过程。随着对汉森不利的证据不断增加，人们相信他会被迫认罪。经过一番协商，他的律师达成了一项协议。如果汉森对谋杀安妮·克鲁特纳、乔安娜·梅西纳、雪莉·莫罗和宝拉·古尔丁的罪行认罪，那么他的妻子和孩子就可以免受广受关注的审判所带来的羞辱和痛苦。

45
00:44:35.000 --> 00:45:54.000
The case would be wrapped up quickly so as to receive little attention from the media and Hansen could serve out his sentence in a federal penitentiary. On February 22, 1984, Hansen's attorney escorted him to a meeting with the prosecution team so he could provide a full confession. Hansen couldn't provide a Clutner Annie's true identity, but he said she was his first murder victim. He'd picked her up from downtown Anchorage and stabbed her to death north of the city. Joanna Messina from Seward was his second. Hansen killed her upon realizing she was a sex worker who had no genuine interest in him. Posing as a high-paying photographer, Hansen lured Sherry Morrow, the first woman he took out to his Canick River Valley hunting grounds. Upon reaching the sandbar that spanned the river, Hansen brought his car to a stop and pulled Sherry out. She wasn't cooperating, so Hansen retrieved his rifle and sat under a tree waiting for her to settle.
案件将迅速了结，以便少受媒体关注，汉森可以在联邦监狱服刑。1984年2月22日，汉森的律师陪同他与控方团队会面，以便他能够供认不讳。汉森无法提供安妮·克鲁特纳的真实身份，但他说她是他的第一个谋杀受害者。他把她从安克雷奇市中心接走，并在该市北部将她刺死。来自苏厄德的乔安娜·梅西纳是他的第二个受害者。汉森意识到她是一名对他没有真正兴趣的性工作者后杀害了她。汉森伪装成一名高薪摄影师，引诱了雪莉·莫罗，她是他带到卡尼克河谷狩猎场的第一个女人。到达横跨河流的沙洲时，汉森把车停下，把雪莉拉了出去。她很不配合，于是汉森取回步枪，坐在树下等她平静下来。

46
00:45:54.000 --> 00:47:00.000
According to Hansen, Sherry stood over him, kicking and screaming, which prompted him to point the rifle up and shoot her. This claim contradicted evidence from the crime scene which showed Sherry was blindfolded and had been shot three times in the back. After burying Sherry in the silt and sand, Hansen left with her arrowhead necklace as a keepsake. Paula Goulding suffered a similar fate in the valley. Then there was survivor Cindy Paulson, who Hansen finally admitted to abducting and raping. He also admitted to the murder of Andrea Altieri, a dancer who had vanished after meeting a man who was going to take her on a shopping spree. Andrea wore a custom-made necklace that featured a pendant in the shape of a fish, given to her by a friend. It was found among the jewelry stored in Hansen's attic.
据汉森称，雪莉站在他上方，又踢又叫，这促使他举起步枪向她射击。这一说法与犯罪现场的证据相矛盾，现场证据显示雪莉被蒙住双眼，背部中枪三枪。将雪莉埋在淤泥和沙子里后，汉森拿走了她的箭头项链作为纪念品。宝拉·古尔丁在山谷中遭遇了类似的命运。然后是幸存者辛迪·保尔森，汉森最终承认绑架并强奸了她。他还承认谋杀安妮塔·阿尔蒂里，一名在遇见一个要带她去血拼的男子后失踪的舞者。安妮塔戴着一条朋友送的定制项链，项链上有一个鱼形吊坠。它在汉森阁楼存放的珠宝中被发现。

47
00:47:00.000 --> 00:48:10.000
Hansen said he abducted Andrea just two weeks after he killed Sherry Morrow. He had driven Andrea, blindfolded and handcuffed, to the Kinnick Valley area and pulled up to an isolated spot near a railroad bridge. Hansen had brought another woman there a week prior and raped her, but ultimately let her go. Andrea endured a similar experience, though hers ended fatally. Hansen claimed Andrea had reached for his pistol, causing them to scuffle. Hansen pried it from her grasp, and as the fight continued, Andrea put her fingers behind Hansen's glasses and pressed them into his eye sockets. In response, Hansen shot her dad. He filled a duffel bag with gravel and tied it around Andrea's neck, before pushing her body off the railroad bridge into the Kinnick River below.
汉森说他在杀死雪莉·莫罗两周后绑架了安妮塔。他开车把被蒙住眼睛、戴上手铐的安妮塔带到基尼克山谷地区，在铁路桥附近的一个偏僻地点停了下来。汉森一周前曾把另一个女人带到那里并强奸了她，但最终放了她。安妮塔经历了类似的遭遇，尽管她的结局是致命的。汉森声称安妮塔伸手去拿他的手枪，导致两人发生争斗。汉森从她手中挣脱手枪，在争斗继续时，安妮塔将手指伸到汉森的眼镜后面，按进他的眼窝。作为回应，汉森开枪打死了她。他在一个行李袋里装满砾石，绑在安妮塔的脖子上，然后将她的尸体从铁路桥推落到下方的基尼克河中。

48
00:48:10.000 --> 00:49:21.000
After Hansen concluded his detailed confession, District Attorney Victor Krum stood. In a no-nonsense tone, Krum informed Hansen that they knew he hadn't been completely honest with them. Hansen's aviation map indicated he had killed many more women. The forests were covered with winter snow, but as soon as spring arrived and the ice thawed, state troopers would be taking sniffer dogs out to every area marked on the map until they found the rest of Hansen's victims. DA Krum Snapped If you think this is the end, we're gonna prosecute you on every one of these cases. There's gonna be a trial for everything. The ordinarily meek and mild-mannered Hansen turned bright red. He looked furious. In a low voice, Hansen muttered, quote, Dirty fucking whores.
汉森详细供认后，地区检察官维克托·克鲁姆站了起来。克鲁姆用不容商榷的语气告诉汉森，他们知道他并没有对他们完全坦白。汉森的航空地图表明他杀害了更多女性。森林里覆盖着冬雪，但一旦春天到来冰雪融化，州骑警就会带着缉毒犬前往地图上标记的每一个地方，直到找到汉森剩下的受害者。地区检察官克鲁姆厉声说道：“如果你认为这就是结束，我们将在所有这些案件中起诉你。每一件事都要接受审判。”平时温和顺从的汉森脸色通红。他看起来暴怒无比。汉森压低声音咕哝道：“该死的婊子。”

49
00:49:21.000 --> 00:50:30.000
Finally, the prosecutors were getting a real look at the men who had attacked and murdered so many women. Another deal was hastily arranged. If Hansen provided further confessions and assisted state troopers in locating his remaining victims, then he would only be charged with the four murders he'd already admitted to. He Agreed Hansen claimed to have killed 17 women, not the 21 investigators suspected due to his map. His victims were always vulnerable women from the Tenderloin District, whose disappearances would be easily overlooked or disregarded by authorities. This systemic prejudice had ensured that Hansen maintained his killing streak without fear of apprehension. Hansen liked to big note himself to the women he abducted, sometimes telling them he was a doctor or a lawyer.
终于，检察官们得以真正看清这个袭击并谋杀如此多女性的男人的真面目。另一项协议仓促达成。如果汉森提供进一步的供词并协助州警定位他剩余的受害者，那么他将只被指控他已经承认的四起谋杀案。他同意了。汉森声称他杀害了17名女性，而不是调查人员根据他的地图怀疑的21人。他的受害者总是来自特德洛因区的弱势女性，她们的失踪很容易被当局忽视或无视。这种系统性的偏见确保了汉森在不用担心被捕的情况下保持他的杀戮狂潮。汉森喜欢在绑架的女性面前吹嘘自己，有时告诉她们自己是医生或律师。

50
00:50:30.000 --> 00:51:33.000
He lured them with large amounts of money, knowing it would be difficult for them to refuse. Hansen tried to convince those questioning him that he wasn't the misogynist they thought he was, explaining that he only targeted women who he felt were inferior to him. Quote I'm not saying that I hate all women. I don't. Quite to the contrary. I guess in my own mind what I'm classifying is a good woman, not a prostitute. I'd do everything in my power, any way, shape or form, to do anything for her, and to see that no harm ever came to her. But I guess prostitutes are women I'm putting down as lower than myself. He assured his interrogators that he hadn't killed every woman he abducted. As long as they went along with what he wanted, he felt fine about letting them live.
他用巨额金钱诱惑她们，深知她们很难拒绝。汉森试图让审讯他的人相信他不是他们想象的那种厌女症患者，并解释说他只针对那些他认为不如自己的女性。引述：“我不是说我恨所有女人。我没有。恰恰相反。我想在我自己的心里，我所归类的是好女人，而不是妓女。我会竭尽全力，以任何方式、形状或形式，为她做任何事，并确保她绝不受伤害。但我想妓女是我认为比我自己地位低的女人。”他向审讯人员保证，他并没有杀死他绑架的每一个女人。只要她们顺从他的意愿，他觉得让她们活下去也无妨。

51
00:51:33.000 --> 00:52:56.000
When they put up a fight or tried to flee, he felt the need to kill, explaining, I guess I wanted to control things. Even though Hansen couldn't remember many of his murder victims' names, the sites where they were buried were still fresh on his mind. He was flown to the areas he'd marked on his map, and according to the book Fair Game, Hansen became noticeably thrilled and exhilarated traversing his former hunting grounds. He triumphantly pointed out where he had left each victim and, quote, A couple of times he became so excited he dropped to his knees to dig in the snow with his hands, looking wide-eyed and with a smile on his flushed, pockmarked face. Those accompanying Hansen were disturbed and angered by his behavior. Promising themselves this would be the last time the killer would ever step foot in the Alaskan wilderness that he so clearly adored. They marked each and every gravesite, then waited patiently for spring so that they could start digging.
当她们反抗或试图逃跑时，他觉得有必要杀人，并解释说：“我想我想要控制一切。”尽管汉森记不清许多谋杀受害者的名字，但她们被埋葬的地点仍然清晰地印在他的脑海里。他被空运到他在地图上标记的区域，根据书《公平竞争》（Fair Game）记载，汉森在穿梭于他以前的狩猎场时变得明显兴奋和激昂。他得意洋洋地指出他把每个受害者留在了哪里，并引述：“有好几次他兴奋得跪倒在地，用双手在雪中挖着，睁大眼睛，在他那张充血、长满痘痕的脸上挂着微笑。”陪同汉森的人对他的行为感到不安和愤怒。他们向自己保证，这将是这个杀手最后一次踏上他显然深爱的阿拉斯加荒野。他们标记了每一个墓地，然后耐心地等待春天以便开始挖掘。

52
00:52:56.000 --> 00:54:01.000
Tuesday, April 24, 1984 marked the first day of the search for Robert Hansen's remaining victims. With shovels in hand, groups of Alaska state troopers gathered around the spots marked on Hansen's map or pointed out by him directly and began digging. On that day, two bodies were found. 22-year-old Sue Luna was uncovered by a creek on the Kinnick River. 28-year-old Malay Larson was in a parking area downriver, a short distance from the old Kinnick Bridge. Over the next couple of days, a further two victims were recovered. The first was an unknown woman found by Horseshoe Lake, further inland and to the northwest of Kinnick River. Aged between 17 and 21 years old, she had been shot and stabbed.
1984年4月24日星期二，搜寻罗伯特·汉森剩余受害者的行动迎来了第一天。阿拉斯加州警手持铁锹，聚集在汉森地图上标记或他直接指出的地点周围，开始挖掘。那一天，发现了两具尸体。22岁的苏·卢娜在基尼克河的一条小溪旁被发掘出来。28岁的马拉·拉尔森在河下游的一个停车场，距离旧基尼克桥不远。在接下来的几天里，又找回了另外两名受害者。第一个是一名身份不明的女性，在基尼克河西北部更内陆的马蹄湖旁被发现。她年龄在17至21岁之间，曾遭枪击和刺伤。

53
00:54:01.000 --> 00:55:17.000
She was white with brown hair and dressed in jeans, a sweater, a coat, scarf and tennis shoes. Hansen couldn't recall her name and despite efforts, investigators were unable to formally identify her. Like a clutner Annie, they named this victim after the area where she was found, Horseshoe Harriet. The second body was that of 24-year-old Angela Fadden. Scavenging animals had reduced her remains to just a jawbone. Three days later, 20-year-old Tammy Peterson was found on an island in the middle of the Kinnick River. 41-year-old Lisa Fertrell was next on May 9, located south of the old Kinnick Bridge. Just over one week later, 22-year-old Teresa Watson was found at Scenic Lake, 30 miles southwest of Anchorage. Bloodhounds were taken to the remaining gravesites pinpointed by Robert Hansen, but had no luck finding anything.
她是白人，留着棕色头发，穿着牛仔裤、毛衣、外套、围巾和网球鞋。汉森想不起她的名字，尽管付出了努力，调查人员仍无法正式确认她的身份。就像安妮·克鲁特纳一样，调查人员以发现她的地区将这位受害者命名为“马蹄哈丽特”。第二具尸体是24岁的安吉拉·法登。食腐动物将她的遗骸啃食得只剩下一块下颌骨。三天后，20岁的塔米·彼得森在基尼克河正中的一个岛上被发现。紧随其后的是5月9日发现的41岁的莉萨·弗特雷尔，位于旧基尼克桥以南。仅仅一周多后，22岁的特雷萨·沃森在安克雷奇西南30英里的风景湖被发现。搜救犬被带到罗伯特·汉森标出的其余墓地，但一无所获。

54
00:55:17.000 --> 00:56:47.000
It was believed that if there were indeed bodies there at one point, they might have since been scavenged by animals or swept away by heavy rains in the sand and silt. In August the following year of 1985, an amateur pilot testing out his aircraft's new tires came into land along the sandbar spanning the Kinnick River. The area was no longer Robert Hansen's hunting ground, but his presence still remained. While there, the pilot discovered human remains. Two handmade rings found on the body led to an identification. It was missing Anchorage woman, 20-year-old DeLynn Frey. She would be known as Hansen's final victim, killed in April 1983, shortly after Paula Goulding. In the wake of Robert Hansen's crimes being publicly revealed, the media dubbed him the Butcher Baker, referencing his years of working as an unremarkable baker while secretly slaughtering women the entire time. The courtroom was packed when Hansen was sentenced for his crimes on Monday, February 27, 1984.
据信，如果那里曾经确实有尸体，它们可能后来已被动物啃食或被沙泥中的大雨冲走。第二年（1985年）8月，一名测试飞机新轮胎的业余飞行员在横跨基尼克河的沙洲旁降落。这个地方不再是罗伯特·汉森的狩猎场，但他的痕迹依然存在。在那里，飞行员发现了人类遗骸。在尸体上发现的两枚手工戒指帮助确认了身份。死者是失踪的安克雷奇20岁女性德林·弗雷。她被称为汉森的最后一名受害者，于1983年4月被杀，紧随宝拉·古尔丁之后。在罗伯特·汉森的罪行被公开曝光后，媒体给他起了个绰号叫“屠夫面包师”，指的是他多年来一直做着一个不起眼的面包师，同时却在暗中屠杀女性。1984年2月27日星期二，汉森因其罪行被判刑时，法庭座无虚席。

55
00:56:47.000 --> 00:58:18.000
Friends and families of the victims made up a large proportion of the spectators. Survivor Cindy Paulson was also there. At no time did Hansen show any remorse for his actions. Assistant District Attorney Frank Rothschild described Hansen as an extreme aberration of a human being, then added, While he doesn't admit it, it's obvious from reading through and looking at where things started and where the women ended up, he hunted them down. He let them run a little bit, and then he enjoyed a little hunt, just like with his big game animals. He toyed with them, he wanted to scare them. He got a charge out of all of this. Rothschild was certain that Hansen was beyond rehabilitation, and requested he be given a life sentence and three separate 99-year terms for the four murders he was charged with. For the rape and abduction of Cindy Paulson, he asked for another 129 years. The presiding judge obliged, sentencing Robert Hansen to 461 years in prison, the maximum possible sentence available in Alaska for his crimes.
受害者的朋友和家属占了旁听席很大一部分。幸存者辛迪·保尔森也在场。汉森自始至终没有对自己的行为表现出任何悔意。助理地区检察官弗兰克·罗斯柴尔德将汉森描述为人性的极端畸变，接着补充道：“虽然他不承认，但从阅读和查看事情的起点以及女性们的最终结局来看，很明显他是在猎杀她们。他让她们跑一小会儿，然后他享受了一场小小的狩猎，就像对待他的大型猎物一样。他戏弄她们，他想吓唬她们。这一切让他感到兴奋。”罗斯柴尔德确信汉森已经不可救药，并请求判处他终身监禁以及因他被指控的四起谋杀案而判处三个独立的99年徒刑。对于强奸和绑架辛迪·保尔森的罪行，他要求再判处129年。主审法官同意了这一请求，判处罗伯特·汉森461年监禁，这是阿拉斯加对其罪行可判处的最高法定刑期。

56
00:58:18.000 --> 00:59:30.000
He noted that even though Hansen's history was well known to authorities, he had been able to kill indiscriminately for years by targeting vulnerable victims. Quote, The court system has failed. If ever there was a case in which a man or defendant needed to be surveilled for the rest of his life, it is this gentleman here, and it's been known for many years. Here, we've turned a person loose several times, knowing he had the propensity for what he did. There's absolutely no excuse for it. I hope when we leave this courtroom today that I have to the best of my ability provided this man shall never walk the streets of America or any other place as a free man. Including a Clutner Annie, Joanna Messina, Sherry Morrow and Paula Goulding, a total of 11 of Robert Hansen's known murder victims have so far been recovered.
他指出，尽管当局对汉森的历史十分了解，但他通过锁定弱势受害者，多年来一直能够不加选择地杀人。“引述：司法系统失败了。如果说有一个案件需要对一个男人或被告进行终身监视，那就是眼前这位绅士，而且这已经广为人知多年了。在这里，我们明知一个人有这种行为倾向，却还是好几次把他放了出去。这绝对没有任何借口。我希望当我们今天离开这个法庭时，我已经尽我所能确保这个男人再也不会以自由人的身份踏上美国的街道或任何其他地方的土地。包括安妮·克鲁特纳、乔安娜·梅西纳、雪莉·莫罗和宝拉·古尔丁在内，罗伯特·汉森已知的谋杀受害者迄今为止共找回了11人。”

57
00:59:30.000 --> 01:00:39.000
According to Hansen's confession, that still leaves six unaccounted for. While Hansen acknowledged that he had killed 23-year-old Andrea Altieri and 24-year-old Roxanne Eastland, they are two of the six victims that were never recovered. To this day, all their cases remain open. Investigators are certain that Hansen is responsible for more murders than he admitted to, given there were four markings on his map that he never addressed. One aligned with the location where 18-year-old Celia Beth Vanz Anton was found on Christmas Day 1971. She had disappeared days earlier after walking to a downtown store to buy a soda. Beth was stripped, bound, gagged and raped before being left in the McHugh Creek Recreation Area, where she froze to death. The crime has never been solved.
根据汉森的供词，这意味着还有6人下落不明。虽然汉森承认他杀害了23岁的安妮塔·阿尔蒂里和24岁的罗克珊·东斯兰，但她们是永远未被找回的6名受害者中的两人。直到今天，她们的案件全部仍然悬而未决。调查人员确信汉森犯下的谋杀案比他承认的还要多，因为他的地图上有四个标记他从未提及。其中一个与1971年圣诞节那天18岁的小采莉亚·贝思·范·安东被发现的地点吻合。她在几天前步行去市中心商店买苏打水后失踪。贝思在被剥光衣服、捆绑、堵嘴和强奸后，被扔在麦克休溪游憩区，在那里冻死。这起犯罪至今未破。

58
01:00:39.000 --> 01:01:54.000
To many, Robert Hansen seems a likely suspect, especially as Beth's ordeal came mere days after Hansen attacked two other women, both of whom survived. Two marks made on the map along Resurrection Bay in the port city of Seward are also unaccounted for. It is believed one represents missing 17-year-old Megan Emmerich. Megan was a student at the Seward Skill Center and was last cited leaving the dormitory laundry room on Saturday July 7, 1973. She hasn't been seen or heard of since. Hansen admitted to being in Seward on the day Megan vanished, but denied crossing paths with her. He also said he was in Seward on Saturday July 5, 1975, when 22-year-old Mary Thill vanished from the city. Although Hansen also denied having any involvement in Mary's disappearance, it has speculated the second Seward-based asterisk hints at her burial location.
在许多人看来，罗伯特·汉森似乎是一个很有嫌疑的嫌疑人，特别是贝思的遭遇恰好发生在汉森袭击另外两名幸存女性几天之后。地图上沿港口城市苏厄德的复活湾制作的两个标记也下落不明。据信其中一个代表失踪的17岁女孩梅根·埃默里奇。梅根是苏厄德技能中心的学生，最后一次被看到是在1973年7月7日星期六离开宿舍洗衣房的时候。此后再也没有人见过或听到她的消息。汉森承认在梅根失踪当天去过苏厄德，但否认与她擦肩而过。他还说自己在1975年7月5日星期六22岁的玛丽·蒂尔在该市失踪时也在苏厄德。尽管汉森也否认自己与玛丽的失踪有任何牵连，但据推测第二个以苏厄德为基地的星号暗示了她的埋尸地点。

59
01:01:54.000 --> 01:03:08.000
Both Megan Emmerich and Mary Thill's cases remain unsolved. Robert Hansen was incarcerated at a number of different penitentiaries before serving the majority of his sentence at a correctional center in Seward. In 2014, he was transferred back to Anchorage to be admitted to Alaska Regional Hospital as he was battling chronic illness. He died on August 21 of that year at the age of 75. By the time of his death, Hansen had admitted to carrying out 30 rapes and 17 murders over a 12-year span, though these numbers remained disputed. Upon learning of Hansen's death, Glenn Flothey told the Anchorage Daily News, On this day, we should only remember his many victims and all of their families, and my heart goes out to all of them. As far as Hansen is concerned, this world is better without him.
梅根·埃默里奇和玛丽·蒂尔的案件至今仍未侦破。罗伯特·汉森曾被关押在多所不同的监狱中，之后在苏厄德的一所惩教中心服完了大部分刑期。2014年，他被转回安克雷奇，由于身患慢性病而被送入阿拉斯加地区医院。他于当年8月21日去世，享年75岁。在他去世时，汉森承认在12年的时间里实施了30起强奸和17起谋杀，尽管这些数字仍存争议。得知汉森的死讯后，格伦·弗洛西告诉《安克雷奇每日新闻》：“在今天，我们应该只记住他的众多受害者和他们所有的家属，我的心与他们所有人同在。至于汉森，这个世界没有他会更好。”

60
01:03:08.000 --> 01:03:13.000
In a 2019 interview for A&E's real crime blog, former Assistant District Attorney Frank Rothschild said that though some wished Hansen could have been given the death penalty, spending his final 30 years in prison had been a fitting end to his life. Here's a guy whose passion in life is going out into the wilderness and hunting the great Alaska wild. Instead of being able to do that, he was put in a cell with no view of anything, forget the mountains, with rancid air and horrific people around him. That, to me, is supreme punishment. There aren't comments yet for this episode. Click on any sentence in the transcript to leave a comment.
在2019年为A&E真实犯罪博客接受采访时，前助理地区检察官弗兰克·罗斯柴尔德表示，尽管有些人希望汉森被判处死刑，但在监狱里度过他最后的30年是他生命的恰当结局。“这是一个生活中的激情在于走进荒野并猎捕阿拉斯加伟大大自然的人。他非但没能做到这一点，反而被关进了一个什么风景也看不到的牢房里，别提什么群山了，周围只有恶臭的空气和可怕的人。对我来说，这就是至高无上的惩罚。”这个剧集还没有评论。点击剧本中的任意句子即可发表评论。
